-- title:
--   §2 (external, Connes–Feldman–Weiss) — a μ-amenable relation in Lodha and Moore's sense is amenable
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a Polish space with its Borel $\sigma$-algebra, $\mu$ a $\sigma$-finite measure, and $E \subseteq X \times X$ a Borel equivalence relation with countable classes such that the $E$-saturation of every $\mu$-null set is $\mu$-null. If $E$ is $\mu$-amenable in Lodha and Moore's sense (`IsMuAmenable`), then $E$ is amenable in the sense of Connes, Feldman and Weiss: it has a left invariant mean (`Monod.IsAmenableRel`).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The $\sigma$-finiteness and quasi-invariance hypotheses are the setting of Connes, Feldman and Weiss; see the note on the converse, `isMuAmenable_of_isAmenableRel`.
-- source:
--   Connes, A., Feldman, J., Weiss, B., An amenable equivalence relation is generated by a single transformation, Ergodic Theory Dynam. Systems 1 (1981) 431–450, https://doi.org/10.1017/S014338570000136X, p. 4, §2

